---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <section class="hero">
    <canvas class="hero-canvas" id="pearl-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="bar" aria-hidden="true"></span>Independent research lab</p>
      <h1>
        <span class="lp"><span style="--i:0">Intelligence, measured.</span></span>
        <span class="lp"><span style="--i:1"><span class="shimmer">Judgment, audited.</span></span></span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Deep Pearl AI studies two sides of the same question: <strong>how do we
        know an AI system actually works</strong> — and how do we know the judge
        grading it is right? Multivac measures frontier models with blind,
        cross-family peer evaluation. PartialCredit measures the judges
        themselves against code that actually runs.
      </p>
      <p class="readout" id="pearl-readout" role="status" aria-live="off">
        <span>NACRE&nbsp;SIM</span>
        <span>LAYER <strong id="ro-layer">00/44</strong></span>
        <span>&Delta;r <strong id="ro-dr">0.00px</strong></span>
        <span>T+<strong id="ro-t">0.0s</strong></span>
      </p>
      <dl class="meta" style="margin-top: 36px">
        <div>
          <dt>Evaluation</dt>
          <dd>Multivac</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Judge audit</dt>
          <dd>PartialCredit</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Status</dt>
          <dd>Paper under review · preregistered study</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="ventures">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-header" data-accrete>
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="bar" aria-hidden="true"></span>The work</p>
        <h2>Two instruments, one thesis</h2>
        <p class="kicker">
          Frontier models are judged by benchmarks they can game, then graded by
          judges nobody has checked. We work both ends of that gap. Each
          instrument below is a working model of its research — open the drawer
          to see it run.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="ventures" data-accrete>
        <article class="venture sheen">
          <div class="specimen"><canvas data-motif="multivac" aria-hidden="true"></canvas></div>
          <div class="venture-body">
            <div class="venture-head">
              <h3>Multivac</h3>
              <span class="tag tag-review">Paper under review</span>
            </div>
            <p class="role">Fig. 1 · The peer matrix</p>
            <p class="desc">
              Independent, blind evaluation of frontier language models. Fresh
              questions models haven't memorized, judged by a cross-family peer
              matrix — no vendor grades its own homework.
            </p>
            <span class="venture-link">Open Multivac <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
          </div>
          <a class="cover" href="/multivac" aria-label="Multivac"></a>
        </article>

        <article class="venture sheen">
          <div class="specimen"><canvas data-motif="partialcredit" aria-hidden="true"></canvas></div>
          <div class="venture-body">
            <div class="venture-head">
              <h3>PartialCredit</h3>
              <span class="tag tag-active">Preregistered · pilot complete</span>
            </div>
            <p class="role">Fig. 2 · The pass vector</p>
            <p class="desc">
              Pairs of partially-correct code fixes, scored by hidden tests, shown
              to LLM judges blind. It measures how often a judge prefers the fix
              that execution says is worse — and whether that rate climbs as the
              two fixes get closer.
            </p>
            <span class="venture-link">Open PartialCredit <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
          </div>
          <a class="cover" href="/partialcredit" aria-label="PartialCredit"></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="superintelligence">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-header" data-accrete>
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="bar" aria-hidden="true"></span>Working note</p>
        <h2>Superintelligence from first principles</h2>
        <p class="kicker">There are many definitions of superintelligence. Here is what we have understood so far.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="si-body" data-accrete>
        <p class="si-lead">Superintelligence is not magic and not a mood. It is a claim about optimization: that a system can be built which is far better than humans at achieving goals across almost every domain.</p>
        <h3 class="si-sub" id="si-essentials-h">Stripped to essentials</h3>
        <ol class="si-essentials" role="list" aria-labelledby="si-essentials-h">
          <li>Intelligence is the ability to achieve goals across many environments.</li>
          <li>Superintelligence greatly exceeds humans at that, in almost every domain.</li>
          <li>Physics permits it. The human brain is a floor, not a ceiling.</li>
          <li>Progress is fast and measured. The timeline is uncertain.</li>
          <li>The brakes are data, energy, experiments, the test to reality gap, and verification.</li>
          <li>The central problem is trust: verifying a mind smarter than the grader.</li>
          <li>Control is layered. No single method is enough.</li>
          <li>Watch time horizons, AI driven research, verifiable discoveries and safety progress.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="callout">
          <p>Using a first principles lens, the deepest question about superintelligence is not whether it can be built. Physics allows it and the trend points toward it. The question is the one Asimov asked in 1956: when the answer comes from something smarter than us, how do we know it is true?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="si-more">
          <a href="/superintelligence">Read the full breakdown <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="principles">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section-header" data-accrete>
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="bar" aria-hidden="true"></span>How we work</p>
        <h2>First principles, honestly reported</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="principles" data-accrete>
        <article class="principle">
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <h3>No one grades their own homework</h3>
          <p>
            Evaluations are blind and judged across model families. A
            benchmark's design shapes its rankings, so we design against our
            own bias first.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <h3>Run the code, then audit the judge</h3>
          <p>
            PartialCredit scores every patch on a hidden, human-authored test
            suite that no judge ever sees. Pass rate is a proxy, so a blind
            manual audit decides whether a disagreement is a judge error, a
            weak test or ambiguous.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <span class="num">03</span>
          <h3>Preregister, then look</h3>
          <p>
            Hypotheses, exclusions and analyses are frozen before the data
            exists, and every change is a dated amendment. Inconclusive is
            published as inconclusive.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* the PartialCredit tag is long: let the card head wrap on narrow cards instead of clipping it */
  .venture-head {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* ---------- superintelligence: the note's opening, essentials and closing ---------- */
  .si-lead {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 48, "SOFT" 30;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.3vw, 25px);
    line-height: 1.32;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--text);
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 0 clamp(32px, 5vh, 48px);
  }

  .si-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faint);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }

  /* the eight points, verbatim: two columns read down the first and then the
     second (01–04, 05–08); one column below the grid breakpoint */
  .si-essentials {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: essential;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    grid-template-rows: repeat(4, auto);
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    column-gap: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px);
  }

  .si-essentials li {
    counter-increment: essential;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 40px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 16px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .si-essentials li::before {
    content: counter(essential, decimal-leading-zero);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--pearl-a);
    padding-top: 3px;
  }

  /* the way on to the full note, in the venture cards' quiet link voice */
  .si-more {
    margin-top: clamp(24px, 4vh, 32px);
  }

  .si-more a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 6px 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    transition: color 140ms ease;
  }

  .si-more a:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .si-more .arrow {
    transition: transform 140ms ease;
  }

  .si-more a:hover .arrow {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .si-essentials {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      grid-template-rows: none;
      grid-auto-flow: row;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import {
    pearlLUT,
    lutColor,
    makeNoise,
    makeSim,
    glowSprite,
    reducedMotion,
  } from '../lib/nacre.js';

  function initHome() {
    const heroCanvas = document.getElementById('pearl-canvas');
    if (!heroCanvas || heroCanvas.dataset.init) return;
    heroCanvas.dataset.init = '1';

    const lut = pearlLUT(undefined, 256, 2.4);
    const { fbm } = makeNoise(7);

    /* ---------------- The Accretion — hero pearl ---------------- */

    const RINGS = 44;
    const light = glowSprite([240, 238, 232], 256, 0.5);
    const core = glowSprite(lut[40], 256, 0.9);
    const roLayer = document.getElementById('ro-layer');
    const roDr = document.getElementById('ro-dr');
    const roT = document.getElementById('ro-t');

    let px = -1;
    let py = -1;
    const hero = heroCanvas.closest('.hero');
    hero.addEventListener(
      'pointermove',
      (e) => {
        const r = heroCanvas.getBoundingClientRect();
        px = e.clientX - r.left;
        py = e.clientY - r.top;
      },
      { passive: true }
    );
    hero.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => {
      px = -1;
      py = -1;
    });

    const easeOut = (t) => 1 - Math.pow(1 - t, 3);
    let roTick = 0;

    function drawPearl(ctx, t, view, still) {
      const { W, H } = view;
      const narrow = W < 700;
      const cx = narrow ? W * 0.5 : W * 0.7;
      const cy = narrow ? H * 0.24 : H * 0.42;
      const R = Math.min(W, H) * (narrow ? 0.34 : 0.42);

      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);

      // light position: cursor, or slow autonomous orbit
      let lx, ly;
      if (px >= 0) {
        lx = px;
        ly = py;
      } else {
        lx = cx + Math.cos(t * 0.00012) * R * 0.8;
        ly = cy + Math.sin(t * 0.00009) * R * 0.6;
      }
      const aim = Math.atan2(ly - cy, lx - cx);

      const grown = still ? RINGS : Math.min(RINGS, easeOut(Math.min(1, t / 2600)) * RINGS);
      const segs = view.degraded ? 56 : 88;

      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'lighter';

      // pearl core
      const coreR = R * 0.5 * (grown / RINGS);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.5;
      ctx.drawImage(core, cx - coreR, cy - coreR, coreR * 2, coreR * 2);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;

      let lastAmp = 0;
      const n = Math.floor(grown);
      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        const br = R * Math.pow((i + 1) / RINGS, 0.92);
        const A = R * 0.05 * (0.4 + i / RINGS);
        lastAmp = A;
        ctx.beginPath();
        for (let s = 0; s <= segs; s++) {
          const th = (s / segs) * Math.PI * 2;
          const sway = px >= 0 || !still ? 1 + 0.45 * Math.cos(th - aim) : 1;
          const r =
            br +
            A *
              sway *
              fbm(
                Math.cos(th) * 1.6 + i * 0.31,
                Math.sin(th) * 1.6,
                (still ? 8000 : t) * 0.00012 + i * 0.07,
                2
              );
          const x = cx + Math.cos(th) * r;
          const y = cy + Math.sin(th) * r;
          s === 0 ? ctx.moveTo(x, y) : ctx.lineTo(x, y);
        }
        ctx.closePath();
        ctx.strokeStyle = lutColor(
          lut,
          (i / RINGS + (still ? 0 : t * 0.00002)) % 1,
          0.13
        );
        ctx.lineWidth = 1;
        ctx.stroke();
      }

      // the light source
      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'screen';
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.32;
      ctx.drawImage(light, lx - 170, ly - 170, 340, 340);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';

      // instrument readout
      if (roLayer && ++roTick % 6 === 0) {
        roLayer.textContent = `${String(n).padStart(2, '0')}/${RINGS}`;
        roDr.textContent = `${lastAmp.toFixed(2)}px`;
        roT.textContent = `${(t / 1000).toFixed(1)}s`;
      }
    }

    makeSim(heroCanvas, {
      render: (ctx, t, dt, view) => drawPearl(ctx, t, view, false),
      renderStill: (ctx, view) => {
        drawPearl(ctx, 8000, view, true);
        if (roLayer) {
          roLayer.textContent = `${RINGS}/${RINGS}`;
          roDr.textContent = '2.20px';
          roT.textContent = '—';
        }
      },
    });

    /* -------------- specimen drawers — card motifs --------------- */

    const motifs = {
      multivac(ctx, v) {
        const { W, H } = v;
        const n = 8;
        const pad = 14;
        const cell = Math.min((W - pad * 2) / n, (H - pad * 2) / n);
        const ox = (W - cell * n) / 2;
        const oy = (H - cell * n) / 2;
        for (let r = 0; r < n; r++) {
          for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {
            const x = ox + c * cell;
            const y = oy + r * cell;
            if (r === c) {
              ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(194,69,47,0.75)';
              ctx.lineWidth = 1;
              ctx.strokeRect(x + 1.5, y + 1.5, cell - 3, cell - 3);
              ctx.beginPath();
              ctx.moveTo(x + 2.5, y + cell - 2.5);
              ctx.lineTo(x + cell - 2.5, y + 2.5);
              ctx.stroke();
              continue;
            }
            const h = (Math.sin(r * 12.9898 + c * 78.233) * 43758.5453) % 1;
            const heat = Math.abs(h);
            ctx.fillStyle = lutColor(lut, (r * n + c) / (n * n), 0.08 + heat * 0.4);
            ctx.fillRect(x + 1.5, y + 1.5, cell - 3, cell - 3);
          }
        }
      },

      partialcredit(ctx, v) {
        const { W, H } = v;
        // two pass vectors: row A above row B, one cell per hidden test input.
        // B's passes are a strict subset of A's (nested), so the bracket between
        // the rows spans the difference in pass counts — the gap.
        const n = 36;
        const pad = 14;
        const gap = 2.2; // bracket zone between the rows, in cells
        const cell = Math.min((W - pad * 2) / n, (H - pad * 2) / (2 + gap));
        const ox = (W - cell * n) / 2;
        const oy = (H - cell * (2 + gap)) / 2;
        const passA = Math.round(n * 0.81);
        const passB = Math.round(n * 0.49);
        const hash = (c) => Math.abs((Math.sin(12.9898 + c * 78.233) * 43758.5453) % 1);
        const rank = new Array(n);
        Array.from({ length: n }, (_, c) => c)
          .sort((a, b) => hash(a) - hash(b))
          .forEach((c, i) => (rank[c] = i));
        const row = (y, passes, shift) => {
          for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {
            const x = ox + c * cell;
            if (rank[c] < passes) {
              ctx.fillStyle = lutColor(lut, (c / n + shift) % 1, 0.35 + hash(c) * 0.4);
              ctx.fillRect(x + 1.5, y + 1.5, cell - 3, cell - 3);
              continue;
            }
            ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(233,230,223,0.35)';
            ctx.lineWidth = 1;
            ctx.strokeRect(x + 1.5, y + 1.5, cell - 3, cell - 3);
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(x + cell * 0.32, y + cell * 0.32);
            ctx.lineTo(x + cell * 0.68, y + cell * 0.68);
            ctx.moveTo(x + cell * 0.68, y + cell * 0.32);
            ctx.lineTo(x + cell * 0.32, y + cell * 0.68);
            ctx.stroke();
          }
        };
        row(oy, passA, 0);
        row(oy + cell * (1 + gap), passB, 0.5);
        // the gap bracket, in ink like the plate's; --alert is kept for inversions
        const x0 = ox + passB * cell + 1.5;
        const x1 = ox + passA * cell - 1.5;
        const ym = oy + cell * (1 + gap / 2);
        const tick = cell * 0.3;
        ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(233,230,223,0.5)';
        ctx.lineWidth = 1;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(x0, ym - tick);
        ctx.lineTo(x0, ym + tick);
        ctx.moveTo(x0, ym);
        ctx.lineTo(x1, ym);
        ctx.moveTo(x1, ym - tick);
        ctx.lineTo(x1, ym + tick);
        ctx.stroke();
      },
    };

    document.querySelectorAll('[data-motif]').forEach((c) => {
      const fn = motifs[c.dataset.motif];
      if (!fn) return;
      const ctx = c.getContext('2d');
      makeSim(c, {
        // first draw on (re)size, so the drawer is never blank before the 1 fps tick
        init: (view) => {
          ctx.setTransform(view.DPR, 0, 0, view.DPR, 0, 0);
          fn(ctx, view);
        },
        render: (ctx, t, dt, view) => {
          ctx.clearRect(0, 0, view.W, view.H);
          fn(ctx, view);
        },
        renderStill: (ctx, view) => fn(ctx, view),
        fps: 1, // effectively static; redraw only on resize ticks
      });
    });
  }

  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initHome);
</script>
